WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.183
Week 1: How Spanish Works. spell a name recognize a stressed syllable build a sustainable study loop

2
00:00:07.183 --> 00:00:18.060
Form and meaning. Applying the form. Use vowels, consonants, capital letters, lowercase letters, and hyphens to decide how each model is written and pronounced.

3
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:43.571
Model set. La a es una vocal fuerte. Escribo mi nombre con mayúscula. ¿Cómo se pronuncia esta palabra? Deletrea tu apellido, por favor. La ortografía y el sonido no siempre coinciden. A is a strong vowel. I write my name with a capital letter. How is this word pronounced? Spell your last name, please. Spelling and sound don't always match.

4
00:00:43.571 --> 00:00:53.701
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:53.701 --> 00:01:06.306
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: spell a name; recognize a stressed syllable; build a sustainable study loop. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:06.306 --> 00:01:32.628
Model language. La a es una vocal fuerte. — A is a strong vowel. Escribo mi nombre con mayúscula. — I write my name with a capital letter. ¿Cómo se pronuncia esta palabra? — How is this word pronounced? Deletrea tu apellido, por favor. — Spell your last name, please. La ortografía y el sonido no siempre coinciden. — Spelling and sound don't always match.

7
00:01:32.628 --> 00:01:42.782
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
